---
permalink: /admin/erasure/
title: "Erasure | Admin"
bodyScripts:
  - src: "/scripts/admin-erasure.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/contact-widget.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/palette.js"
    type: "module"
---
<section class="app-page">
  <div class="app-prose">

    {% include "chrome/admin-sections.njk" %}

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-2">Erasure</h1>
    <p class="text-brand-muted mb-6">
      Everything held for one email address, and the one way to remove it. The contact form
      promises a message can be deleted on request and
      <a href="https://tzortzoglou.eu/privacy/" class="text-brand-accent underline hover:no-underline">the privacy
      notice</a> promises Article 17; this is where that gets carried out.
    </p>
    {# Said on the page and not only in the results, because it is the thing an operator needs to
       know BEFORE they promise somebody their data is gone. A contact message is stored and also
       emailed: this screen reaches the database, and nothing reaches the copy that was sent. #}
    <p class="text-brand-muted mb-6">
      It cannot reach the copies that were emailed. Those are shown on every answer below, because
      an erasure that reported "done" while a copy sat in a mailbox would be a lie.
    </p>

    <div id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="mb-6 text-sm"></div>

    <!-- Step 1: look up ------------------------------------------------------ -->
    <form id="lookupForm" method="post" novalidate class="card">
      <label for="target" class="field-label">Email address</label>
      <input spellcheck="false" type="email" id="target" name="target" autocomplete="off"
        maxlength="254" aria-describedby="lookupHint" class="field">
      <p id="lookupHint" class="hint">
        Reads only. Nothing is deleted by looking, and the address is matched the way the API
        matches it: trimmed, and ignoring case.
      </p>
      <button type="submit" class="btn-primary mt-4">Look up</button>
    </form>

    <!-- What is held -------------------------------------------------------- -->
    <div id="held" class="hidden">

      <section aria-labelledby="held-heading" class="card mt-6">
        <h2 id="held-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">
          What is held for <span id="heldWho" class="break-all"></span>
        </h2>

        <h3 class="mt-4 font-semibold text-brand-text">Contact messages</h3>
        <p id="heldMessages" class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
        {# The dates and nothing else. The preview endpoint deliberately returns no IP address and
           no user agent: this screen exists to delete somebody's data, and reading the rest of it
           on the way past is not part of that. #}
        <div id="heldDates" class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"></div>

        <h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-brand-text">Account</h3>
        <p id="heldAccount" class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
        <ul id="heldAccountFacts" class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm text-brand-muted"></ul>
      </section>

      <!-- The out-of-reach copies, as their own block on the preview and again on the receipt. -->
      <section aria-labelledby="reach-heading" class="card mt-4">
        <h2 id="reach-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">Copies this cannot reach</h2>
        <p id="reachCount" class="mt-2 text-sm text-brand-text"></p>
        {# The API's own sentence, printed as it arrives. It is the one part of this page that is
           a statement about systems outside it, so it is not rephrased here - a rewrite would
           drift from what the server actually knows, and this is exactly the claim that must
           not drift. #}
        <p id="reachNote" class="mt-2 text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 2: erase ----------------------------------------------------- -->
      <section id="erase" class="hidden card mt-4" aria-labelledby="erase-heading">
        <h2 id="erase-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">Erase</h2>
        <p class="hint">
          Removes the messages, the stored profile and the sign-in account. It crosses three
          stores, there is no undo, and nothing here can recreate the account.
        </p>

        <button type="button" id="eraseOpen" class="btn-secondary mt-4">Erase what is held…</button>

        {# Red rather than the amber the account page uses for handing an account to another
           address. That action can at least be undone by whoever receives it; this one cannot be
           undone by anybody. The alphas are pitched against a white card, the same way the amber
           panel's were: /60 on the border reads as an edge worth noticing without the panel
           turning into a block of colour. #}
        <div id="eraseConfirm" class="hidden mt-4 rounded-lg border border-red-600/60 bg-red-600/10 p-4">
          {# Names the counts rather than asking "are you sure": the number of messages is the
             fact worth checking, and a dialog that only asks trains people to press yes. #}
          <p class="text-sm text-brand-text">
            About to delete <span id="eraseWhat" class="font-semibold"></span>.
          </p>
          <p class="hint mt-2">
            Type the address to confirm. It is the only address this will act on.
          </p>
          <label for="eraseTyped" class="sr-only">Type the address to confirm</label>
          <input spellcheck="false" type="text" id="eraseTyped" name="eraseTyped" autocomplete="off"
            maxlength="254" class="field mt-2">
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <button type="button" id="eraseGo" class="btn-primary text-sm" disabled>Yes, erase it</button>
            <button type="button" id="eraseCancel" class="btn-secondary text-sm">Cancel</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

    <!-- The receipt --------------------------------------------------------- -->
    <div id="receipt" class="hidden">
      <section aria-labelledby="receipt-heading" class="card mt-6">
        <h2 id="receipt-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">
          Removed for <span id="receiptWho" class="break-all"></span>
        </h2>
        {# Every line under here is built from the erase response, never from the preview. The
           preview is a guess that was true a moment ago; the receipt is what the API says it
           actually deleted, and when the two disagree the receipt is the true one. #}
        <ul id="receiptLines" class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm text-brand-text"></ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="left-heading" class="card mt-4">
        <h2 id="left-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">What is still out there</h2>
        <p id="leftCount" class="mt-2 text-sm text-brand-text"></p>
        <p id="leftNote" class="mt-2 text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
        {# Filled in and revealed only when there were emailed copies. Finishing the job means
           opening the mailbox and deleting them by hand, so the page hands over the search
           instead of leaving the operator to compose it. #}
        <p id="leftSearch" class="hidden mt-3 text-sm"></p>
      </section>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
